                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0819b005-4d41-440f-9cec-496b1a56089b",
                        "source_entry_id": "30834553-1959-3920-980f-043785fa74a5",
                        "source_sense_id": "a5f306cd-5848-33c6-9412-9125768f22bf",
                        "target_lang_word": "assiduously",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "assiduously",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6aed5ee1-9f5e-3345-bf11-2fdfa4fe436f",
                                        "entry_id": "e337e1e3-a5bb-3de6-913a-4694f9805bb3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an assiduous manner; diligently, industriously."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5786e5c-9b9a-4891-b77a-2e87fd30cefe",
                                                "sense_id": "6aed5ee1-9f5e-3345-bf11-2fdfa4fe436f",
                                                "text": "He who had appeared rather assiduously to shun her, whose good opinion she had valued, notwithstanding his seeming indifference to her, had now declared himself, and given proofs of a regard the most unequivocal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b071203b-111d-4a31-a14a-83ea28c346fb",
                                                "sense_id": "6aed5ee1-9f5e-3345-bf11-2fdfa4fe436f",
                                                "text": "They were all too assiduously engaged to talk to us as we passed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1a68209-8462-4e4b-9674-5d8f2b1b0094",
                                                "sense_id": "6aed5ee1-9f5e-3345-bf11-2fdfa4fe436f",
                                                "text": "There were many wooden chairs for the bulk of his visitors, and two wicker arm-chairs with red cloth cushions for superior people. From the packing-cases had also emerged some Indian clubs,[…]; and all these articles[…]made a scattered and untidy decoration that Mrs. Clough assiduously dusted and greatly cherished."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1017c158-f43f-422e-bd0f-43fb4e0a2900",
                                                "sense_id": "6aed5ee1-9f5e-3345-bf11-2fdfa4fe436f",
                                                "text": "Her voice caught in her throat and another violent shiver ran through her. Bradly thought she was going to cry and became actively disturbed, holding her with one arm and patting her shoulder assiduously. \"Damme, don't think about it, Cora.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6ad262d-0587-47e0-a182-f97859a8bdba",
                                                "sense_id": "6aed5ee1-9f5e-3345-bf11-2fdfa4fe436f",
                                                "text": "No. 21C9 was in need of a boiler washout and though she was carefully and assiduously fired and use made of the fire-irons during the run, it was not possible to maintain steam, which often fell as low as 210 lb."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7434e76b-920a-4a50-9f43-65a221c7802b",
                                                "sense_id": "6aed5ee1-9f5e-3345-bf11-2fdfa4fe436f",
                                                "text": "While it remains a burden assiduously avoided, it is not unexpected, and thus not beyond a measure of control. Which has led you, inexorably, here."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c81a99a5-5938-4fdd-973f-e19641082582",
                                                "sense_id": "6aed5ee1-9f5e-3345-bf11-2fdfa4fe436f",
                                                "text": "2020, Frank Bowman, The role of the chief justice in an impeachment trial, SCOTUSblog (Jan. 10, 2020, 11:18 AM), online\nWhat little precedent we have in such cases suggests that chief justices keep their heads down and, so far as possible, defer assiduously to the will of the Senate majority."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "68735185-4535-4f65-981a-a9f5432f0725",
                        "source_entry_id": "30834553-1959-3920-980f-043785fa74a5",
                        "source_sense_id": "a5f306cd-5848-33c6-9412-9125768f22bf",
                        "target_lang_word": "assidûment",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "assidûment",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48da9021-ae83-3c92-aa66-428f73e85902",
                                        "entry_id": "a667a081-66db-3d01-b89f-ddd66cf98f8b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "D’une manière assidue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1fbb03c-fd6a-4d73-92fd-595a8716672a",
                                                "sense_id": "48da9021-ae83-3c92-aa66-428f73e85902",
                                                "text": "Après avoir répondu, dans un premier temps, à son frère, en contre-argumentant, l’auteur a notamment décidé d’infiltrer les deux organisations qu’il suit assidûment, afin de lui montrer qu’elles ne sont pas ce qu’elles prétendent être."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89836b4d-fe9d-4efb-8a90-9c391ec81ad1",
                                                "sense_id": "48da9021-ae83-3c92-aa66-428f73e85902",
                                                "text": "Allez, et que partout on veille assidûment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d65fe808-a75d-427f-b11a-d48575489e3f",
                                                "sense_id": "48da9021-ae83-3c92-aa66-428f73e85902",
                                                "text": "Le résultat est vivement commenté dans la salle de rédaction du « Journal des Débats » où Galliffet, qui inspire le chroniqueur militaire du journal quand il ne dicte pas les articles, fréquente assidûment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35c3aaa8-0b2b-4711-a096-1350ea0e2712",
                                                "sense_id": "48da9021-ae83-3c92-aa66-428f73e85902",
                                                "text": "Lorsque les enfants se sont mis à fréquenter l’école assidûment, ils se sont fait corriger la langue utilisée dans leur famille."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c426f65-30e8-48e5-98f3-c11b1002deaf",
                                                "sense_id": "48da9021-ae83-3c92-aa66-428f73e85902",
                                                "text": "Vous n’avez pas suivi assidûment les 6 premières journées du championnat belge ? Pas de problème, on vous résume ça en quelques points."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
